.TH CHRONICLE.CONF 5 "2026-07-24" "chronicle 1.0" "InterGenOS System Administration"
.SH NAME
chronicle.conf \- Chronicle configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/chronicle/chronicle.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I chronicle.conf
holds the user-tunable
.B policy
for the Chronicle backup engine
.BR chronicled (8).
It is an INI file with a single
.B [chronicle]
section. Every key is optional \(em an absent or partial file yields a usable
default policy, and a malformed value for one key falls back to that key's
default rather than aborting the engine.
.PP
Runtime state the engine owns (the monotonic version sequence, the adopted
target's details, the pin set) lives in
.I /var/lib/chronicle/state.json
and is
.B not
configured here.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR work_start ", " work_end
Working hours as \fBHH:MM\fR (24-hour). The off-peak window \(em when large,
deferred captures drain \(em is the complement of [\fIwork_start\fR,
\fIwork_end\fR). An overnight span (start > end) is supported. Defaults
\fB09:00\fR / \fB18:00\fR.
.TP
.B size_floor_bytes
Absolute change-size floor above which a capture is deferred to off-peak.
Default \fB1073741824\fR (~1 GiB).
.TP
.B free_fraction
Fraction of target free space above which a capture is deferred. The effective
deferral threshold is the
.B smaller
of this and \fIsize_floor_bytes\fR. Default \fB0.05\fR (~5%).
.TP
.B target_device
Preferred whole-volume target (e.g. a
.IR /dev/disk/by-uuid/ ...
path).
.TP
.B target_directory
Preferred directory-class target: a POSIX directory Chronicle owns a capped
subtree under. Use this
.B or
.IR target_device ,
not both.
.TP
.B target_size_cap_bytes
Size cap for the directory-class target's subtree.
.TP
.B target_encryption
Whether to recommend a LUKS2 container on the target so a lost drive is not a
data breach (\fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR). Default \fBtrue\fR.
.TP
.B user_data_paths
Comma-separated home trees to protect. Default \fB/home\fR.
.TP
.B exclude_globs
Comma-separated fnmatch globs excluded from user-data capture. Default excludes
caches and trash (\fB*/.cache/*, */.local/share/Trash/*, */.thumbnails/*\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.nf
[chronicle]
work_start = 08:00
work_end = 17:30
size_floor_bytes = 536870912
target_directory = /run/media/ada/backup
target_size_cap_bytes = 274877906944
exclude_globs = */.cache/*, */node_modules/*
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chronicle (1),
.BR chronicled (8)
